@tradition captains-address
// EW1 (events writer), 2026-10-20: DRAFT words for the Captain's Friday address (plans/fridays-plan.md, part C).
// Not in content/traditions yet: the traditions engineer gives it its k:, checks the rules below against the plan and
// moves it in when SHORT_FRIDAY is built. The speech itself is in content/addresses/friday-*.address (Days 5, 12, 19,
// 26); after Day 26 the weekly shape takes over (not written yet).
// Rules from the plan (rev 4), for the engineer: weekly friday, 16:00-16:50, the auditorium (rec-aud seats), Marrow at
// rec:lectern with Vance beside her; everyone 90%, night shift 50%, the skeleton (helm and watch ratings on the bridge,
// a medic on call, the dinner cooks) never; missing it is a small work-reputation dip (not on leave, sick, a rota day
// off, Dev-mode excused or nights).
k: (the traditions engineer's)
title: The Captain's Friday address
when: weekly friday
at: 16:00-16:50
where: 7 room Auditorium: rec:seat
hold: none
who: marrow always, vance always, night-shift 50%, everyone 90%
host: marrow
from: marrow

== mail
// the evening-before Mail, Thursdays at 18:00. The first one (Day 4, your first week) is the plan's own words.
? week1:true
- Tomorrow's a short Friday. The day shift stops at half past three; I'll see all of you in the auditorium at four. Dinner at five. Our new hands especially.
?
- Tomorrow's a short Friday: the day shift stops at half past three. The Captain's address is at four in the rec deck auditorium. Dinner at five.

== ask
- Captain at four. Back row's mine. Don't tell anyone.   #funny
- Half three, clock out, then the auditorium. Coming?
- She always says one thing you remember all week. Come and hear it.   #warm

== here
- Shh. She's starting.
- Good turnout. She'll notice. She notices everything.
- Budge up. There's a seat by me.

== thanks
- You find a seat in the auditorium as Captain Marrow steps up to the lectern. Commander Vance stands beside her.

== chatter
- Did you hear the Captain's address? She named the galley again.   #warm
- "Those of you who have one." She says it every Friday. I wait for it.   #funny
- Best part of a Friday: half three. Second best: the Captain.
- Short Friday tomorrow. I've already planned my extra hour. It's a nap.   #funny
